BetterGuac for Debian
=====================

Debian 13: FreeRDP from trixie-backports
-----------------------------------------
BetterGuac needs FreeRDP 3.32.2 or later (Debian 13 ships 3.15.0). Install it
from Debian's official backports together with the package:

    echo "deb http://deb.debian.org/debian trixie-backports main" | \
        sudo tee /etc/apt/sources.list.d/trixie-backports.list
    sudo apt update
    sudo apt install ./betterguac_<version>_<arch>.deb libfreerdp3-3/trixie-backports \
        libfreerdp-client3-3/trixie-backports libwinpr3-3/trixie-backports

Ubuntu 26.04 already has FreeRDP 3.32.2.

Sign in
-------
Open http://<this machine>:8080/betterguac/ (or just http://<this machine>:8080/) and sign in as the first
administrator. If you didn't type a password during installation, it is in
/etc/betterguac/initial-admin.txt (root only):

    sudo cat /etc/betterguac/initial-admin.txt

This first account is a setup administrator: it signs in with the password only
and is not asked to enroll two-factor. Create your real administrator accounts
with it, then disable it or keep it as a break-glass account, and delete
initial-admin.txt. The full documentation is in
/usr/share/doc/betterguac/README.md.

Forgot the password:  sudo betterguac-admin reset-password <username>

Where things are
----------------
/etc/betterguac/guacamole.properties  web app settings and database login (root:tomcat 640)
/etc/betterguac/guacd.conf            guacd settings
/etc/betterguac/keys/                 SSH private keys, given to servers by path
                                      (each key: owner root, group tomcat, mode 640)
/etc/betterguac/betterguac.yaml       YAML servers and users (starter file)
/etc/betterguac/sync.env         database login for the YAML sync (root only)
/usr/share/betterguac/                web application, extensions, schema, examples
/usr/lib/betterguac/guacd/            guacd and its protocol plugins

Services: betterguac-guacd, betterguac-web (the web app on the Apache
          Tomcat 10.1 release in /usr/share/betterguac/tomcat), mariadb.
Logs:     journalctl -u betterguac-guacd, journalctl -u betterguac-web,
          /var/log/tomcat10/
Tomcat:   settings in /etc/tomcat10 (server.xml: port 8080), base in
          /var/lib/tomcat10. Your own JAVA_OPTS or CATALINA_OPTS go in
          /etc/default/betterguac-web.
Status:   sudo betterguac-admin status

Adding an SSH key
-----------------
    sudo install -o root -g tomcat -m 640 mykey /etc/betterguac/keys/web-01

Then use /etc/betterguac/keys/web-01 as the server's key file.

Removing
--------
sudo apt remove betterguac   removes the program; settings, keys and the
                             database stay for a later reinstall.
sudo apt purge betterguac    also removes /etc/betterguac (keys included)
                             and the betterguac databases. A copy of the
                             database is saved first in
                             /var/backups/betterguac-purge-<date>.sql.gz.

MariaDB, FreeRDP and the Java runtime stay installed; remove them with
"sudo apt autoremove" if nothing else uses them.
